{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122149","id":4216150608,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc77TVpQ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122149","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122149.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122149.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122149","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122149/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122149/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122149/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/ebe0fec6e14f80ae1ceb45b072276d6b743000f7","number":122149,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"TextEdit: Make scrolling & zooming while selecting more responsive","user":{"login":"NoNormalDev","id":190293561,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1emOQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190293561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev","html_url":"https://github.com/NoNormalDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NoNormalDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCurrently, when the mouse isn't moving, the selection updates on a timer than runs 20 times a second. This obviosely isn't that smooth on a high refresh rate display like 120 hz.\r\n\r\nNow it also updates when the mouse scrolls, and on some other events. That means that it updates when needed, so up to 120 times a second on a 120 Hz screen. You can see this a little bit in the video, but the diffrence on 60 FPS isn't as big (but still very noticable in person).\r\n\r\n## Before\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d907a528-aba4-49e2-90f6-d1ea83a95b26\r\n\r\n## After\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18ea7974-4195-4839-afe3-f495b0298ca4\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nAlso removed some relevant dead code:\r\n\r\n1) `->set_value` already calls `_scroll_moved`, and the input parameter to it isn't even used in the actual method.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n void TextEdit::set_v_scroll(double p_scroll) {\r\n        v_scroll->set_value(p_scroll);\r\n-       int max_v_scroll = v_scroll->get_max() - v_scroll->get_page();\r\n-       if (p_scroll >= max_v_scroll - 1.0) {\r\n-               _scroll_moved(v_scroll->get_value());\r\n-       }\r\n        queue_accessibility_update();\r\n }\r\n```\r\n\r\n2) `0.0` is the default minimum value for `Range`, and isn't modified anywhere, so even if `p_scroll` is negative, `set_value` clamps it to 0. If we want to keep this redundent check, it should be added to `set_v_scroll` aswell for consistency.\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n void TextEdit::set_h_scroll(int p_scroll) {\r\n-       if (p_scroll < 0) {\r\n-               p_scroll = 0;\r\n-       }\r\n        h_scroll->set_value(p_scroll);\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf these are far too out-of-scope for this PR, I'll happily remove them.\r\n\r\nNo AI was used.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archiv